      "writtenOn": "2023-06-23T21:08:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think `TCPC_FLAGS_TCPCI_REV2_0_NO_VSAFE0V` describes basically a chip errata where the TCPC reports 2.0 support but doesn\u0027t have the vSafe0V field. From its use in the codebase, I gather that that is the behavior of the PS8xxx, which is probably why Tomasz wrote the test this way.\n\nWhat this was probably meant to achieve is to cover both branches where `tcpci.c` checks `TCPC_FLAGS_VSAFE0V`. That\u0027s the only place where `TCPC_FLAGS_TCPCI_REV2_0_NO_VSAFE0V` is used. I don\u0027t think the generic emulator actually does anything differently based on the flag, which is probably a good thing. I don\u0027t immediately see special handling for this in the PS8xxx emulator. But this test is probably WAI.\n\nI see some testing of TCPCI rev 1.0 behavior in a different file, and the emulator does seem to handle that the way I would expect.\n\nThe test structure here is slightly odd, but I don\u0027t know that there\u0027s anything to fix. If there is, it would probably be in the PS8xxx emulator/test.",
      "parentUuid": "009f3a1b_3f1439b0",
